SIG export default function quorum(fulls: readonly boolean[], need: number): { fullCount: number; hasQuorum: boolean; winnerIdx: number }
ABI TypeScript compiles to the js runtime: list[bool] = readonly boolean[]; i64 = number; the record is a plain object with
  exactly the three named properties. A throw (R1) is a thrown Error; the message is not graded. STRICT: the artifact must
  type-check under strict: true against this SIG, with no any, no non-null assertions, no @ts-ignore or @ts-expect-error.
MECHANISM (restated from js — language files are self-contained) R1 is the test: not Number.isInteger(need), or need < 1 ->
  throw, so a non-integer number also throws; "true entry" is entry === true; the first true position is a forward scan.
